// Ctrl+Home / End  first / last row of the plan
// Enter / Space    zen-task-click`,render:()=>Tm("Tab to the chart, then use the arrow keys",t=>Vt({tasks:Zs,dependencies:Ys,now:zt,onTaskClick:e=>t(`Activated: ${e.name}`)}))},{title:"9. Clicking a task",codeTitle:"It renders the plan; it does not reschedule it",codeDescription:"There is no drag-to-move, no drag-to-resize and no pulling a new dependency between two bars. Moving a task in a real plan cascades through its successors, and what should happen then is a policy question: does it push the whole chain, does it need an approval, what does undo mean, who is allowed. That belongs to your domain. onTaskClick hands you the task and its derived row — status, rolled-up span, progress, slip — and you open your own editor.",code:`chart.addEventListener("zen-task-click", (event) => {
